  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "On 7 November 2026, 24-year-old Michał Oksiński opened fire from his car in the Main Square in Kraków, Poland, killing six people and injuring 16 others.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385329913:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "Around 14:59 CET that day, a black 3rd generation Subaru Impreza hatchback with an Ostrowiec Świętokrzyski number plate entered the Main Square from Sławkowska Street.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1385329913:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The 24-year-old man responsible for the drive-by mass shooting died at a hospital two days ago after being seriously wounded in a shootout with police.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-09:2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:30Z",
      "text": "As Wikipedia records them, the casualties number 10: 7 in Kraków, including the perpetrator, and 3 at the perpetrator's home in Ostrowiec Świętokrzyski; the injured number 16.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:box:1385329913:casualties",
        "wiki:box:1385329913:injured"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:41Z",
      "text": "On 9 November 2026, the English article drew 114,724 readers; in the 8 to 60 days before, it had none, as it is a new article.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_Kraków_shooting:2026-11-09",
        "views:en:2026_Kraków_shooting:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-09T00:00:48Z",
      "text": "The article is read in 11 languages, and after English the largest readership is in Polish, with 36,015 readers.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:2026_Kraków_shooting:2026-11-09",
        "views:pl:Strzelanina_w_Krakowie_(2026):2026-11-09"
      ]
    },
    {
